# One-rule SELinux module for hosts where the keeper unit cannot open its outbound HTTPS connection.
#
# Symptom: refused_to_start reason="eth_chainId could not be read: AggregateError (EACCES)" and
#   avc: denied { name_connect } scontext=system_u:system_r:init_t:s0 tcontext=system_u:object_r:http_port_t:s0
# in `ausearch -m avc`. The unit's NoNewPrivileges=yes keeps the process in systemd's own init_t domain
# (no domain transition is allowed with NNP), and the targeted policy does not let init_t connect to
# http_port_t (80, 443 and the HTTP alternates). Everything else the keeper needs is already allowed.
#
# Install (keeper/README.md, host setup step 6):
#   checkmodule -M -m -o /tmp/luckydraw_keeper_https.mod keeper/deploy/luckydraw-keeper-https.te
#   semodule_package -o /tmp/luckydraw_keeper_https.pp -m /tmp/luckydraw_keeper_https.mod
#   sudo semodule -i /tmp/luckydraw_keeper_https.pp
# Remove: sudo semodule -r luckydraw_keeper_https
module luckydraw_keeper_https 1.0;

require {
    type init_t;
    type http_port_t;
    class tcp_socket name_connect;
}

allow init_t http_port_t:tcp_socket name_connect;
